.TH NGS3FS 1 "August 2026" "ngs3fs 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ngs3fs \- low-latency S3 FUSE client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ngs3fs
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ "FUSE options" ]
.I mountpoint
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ngs3fs
mounts one S3 bucket or key prefix using the Linux kernel page cache. It is
optimized for buffered and mmap-heavy reads. HTTP/2 is preferred and HTTP/1.1
is detected automatically.
.PP
Writes replace an object from offset zero and must be strictly sequential.
Writable mmap, O_RDWR, O_DIRECT, random overwrite, symbolic links and hard
links are unsupported. FUSE writeback cache must remain disabled.
.PP
Without a local cache, fsync is intentionally non-durable. With --cache-dir,
fsync synchronizes the locally authoritative data and recovery metadata but
does not publish the S3 object. The first flush publishes and permanently seals
a writable handle. Applications must check close errors and must not continue
writing through descriptors retained by dup or fork after any close.
.SH REQUIRED OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-e, --endpoint-host " host
Network host of the S3 endpoint.
.TP
.BI "-b, --bucket " bucket
S3 bucket name.
.SH CONNECTION OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-p, --endpoint-port " port
Endpoint port. Port 443 enables TLS automatically.
.TP
.BI "-a, --authority " authority
HTTP authority, normally a virtual-hosted bucket endpoint.
.TP
.BI "-r, --region " region
SigV4 region. Default is us-east-1.
.TP
.BI "--expected-bucket-owner " account
Send and sign the expected S3 bucket-owner account on every request.
.TP
.B --requester-pays
Send and sign the S3 requester-pays acknowledgement on every request.
.TP
.B -S, --tls
Require TLS on a non-443 port.
.TP
.BI "--connect-timeout " milliseconds
TCP connection timeout. Default is 5000.
.TP
.BI "--request-timeout " milliseconds
No-I/O-progress timeout for active requests. Default is 30000.
.TP
.BI "--protocol-probe-timeout " milliseconds
Maximum cleartext HTTP/2 detection wait. Default is 1000.
.TP
.BI "--metadata-timeout " milliseconds
Per-attempt ECS, IMDS and credential endpoint timeout. Default is 1000.
.TP
.BI "--stats-interval " seconds
Emit aggregate JSON health and resource counters to stderr. Zero disables it.
.SH CACHE AND I/O OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "--io-size " bytes
Preferred I/O size reported by statfs. Default is 256 KiB.
.TP
.BI "-R, --read-ahead " bytes
Requested kernel BDI read-ahead. Default is 256 KiB.
.TP
.BI "-T, --dir-cache-timeout " milliseconds
Directory cache lifetime. Default is 1000.
.TP
.BI "-I, --max-cached-inodes " count
Soft inode cache limit. Default is 1000000.
.TP
.BI "-L, --cache-dir " path
Enable the persistent sparse local data cache at path. Disabled by default.
.TP
.BI "--cache-size " bytes
Maximum physical cache allocation. Zero means no fixed limit.
.TP
.BI "--cache-reserve " size-or-percent
Free space preserved on the cache filesystem. Default is 5%.
.TP
.BI "--max-cache-fetch-size " bytes
Maximum adaptive cache fill. Default is 8 MiB; the minimum is 1 MiB and the
value must be page aligned.
.SH WRITE OPTIONS
.TP
.BI "-P, --part-size " bytes
Multipart part size from 5 MiB through 5 GiB. Default is 8 MiB.
.TP
.BI "-c, --max-uploads " count
Concurrent uploads. Default is 4.
.TP
.BI "-C, --max-connections " count
Connection pool size; it must exceed max-uploads. Default is 8.
.TP
.BI "-B, --max-pinned-memory " bytes
Mount-global retained pipe payload budget. Default is 256 MiB.
.TP
.BI "-K, --checksum " algorithm
Upload checksum. Values include auto, default, none, crc32, crc32c,
crc64nvme, sha1, sha256, md5, xxhash64, xxhash3, xxhash128, sha512 and
crc64xz.
.TP
.B --verify-read-checksum
Enable background best-effort verification of complete independently
verifiable units. The first read or mmap fault may finish before verification.
.SH CREDENTIALS
Credential precedence is AWS environment variables, Web Identity, the selected
shared profile, credential_process, ECS/EKS container credentials and IMDSv2.
Refreshable credentials are renewed before expiration. AWS_PROFILE,
AWS_SHARED_CREDENTIALS_FILE and AWS_CONFIG_FILE are honored. AssumeRole and SSO
profiles should export credentials through credential_process.
.SH FILE ATTRIBUTES
UID, GID, file mode and directory mode are mount-wide and selected with
--uid, --gid, --file-mode and --dir-mode.
.SH SIGNALS AND LOGGING
Warnings and failures are written to stderr. With --metrics, each read emits a
JSON line containing latency and transport counters. Likely random-read advice
is reported at most once per minute. --stats-interval reports remote read and
FUSE write counts and bytes, callback errors, inode/open-handle counts, retained
pipe bytes, copied-write bytes and the active credential source.
.SH PRODUCTION NOTES
Configure the bucket AbortIncompleteMultipartUpload lifecycle rule. Select a
part size large enough that the largest expected object uses at most 10000
parts. Empty directory markers can be renamed as one object. Renaming a
non-empty directory returns EXDEV so callers can use cross-filesystem
copy/remove semantics; ngs3fs does not emulate an atomic S3 prefix rename
operation.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fusermount3 (1),
.BR mount.fuse3 (8)
